  "worked_solution": "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}) & =L({y}_{1})+2L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}\u2061x+2\\cdot ({sin}^{2}\u2061x+4) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}\u2061x+2{sin}^{2}\u2061x+8 \\\\  & =2({cos}^{2}\u2061x+{sin}^{2}\u2061x)+8 \\\\  & =2+8 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
